## CICIoMT2024 dataset

Training and evaluation use the Wi-Fi / MQTT slice of **CICIoMT2024**, published
by the Canadian Institute for Cybersecurity (CIC), University of New Brunswick.

CIC's dataset FAQ states that you may redistribute, republish, and mirror CIC
datasets, but **any use or redistribution must include a citation** to the
dataset and the listed research paper. See:

- https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/iomt-dataset-2024.html
- https://www.unb.ca/cic/datasets/

This repository does **not** ship raw PCAPs (`data/raw/` is gitignored). Obtain
the corpus from CIC and cite:

Dadkhah, S., Neto, E. C. P., Ferreira, R., Molokwu, R. C., Sadeghi, S., &
Ghorbani, A. A. (2024). CICIoMT2024: A benchmark dataset for multi-protocol
security assessment in IoMT. *Internet of Things*, 28, 101351.
https://doi.org/10.1016/j.iot.2024.101351

## Derived model artifact

`artifacts/v1/H0_full_fit.joblib` is a model trained on CICIoMT2024-derived
window features. It is checked in so the serving image is reproducible. It is
**not** MIT-licensed original source; treat it as a derived research artifact
and keep the CIC citation if you redistribute it.

Do not treat this detector as a certified medical-device security product.
